- **`from_montgomery_loop_spec`** (`@[progress]`): given `i.val ≤ 5`, for every `j < 9` the result limb `r[j]` equals the value of `self[j]` (widened to `u128`) when `i ≤ j < 5`. Otherwise it is unchanged from the input `limbs[j]`. The proof works by recursion on `5 - i`.
- **`from_montgomery_loop_zero_spec`**: covers the exact call `from_montgomery` makes, which starts from the all-zero array at index 0. It shows:
  - every limb is below 2^64;
  - limbs 0–4 hold `self`'s limbs and limbs 5–8 are 0;
  - `U128x9_as_Nat r = Scalar52_as_Nat self`.

This gives the next step what `montgomery_reduce_spec` needs: the per-limb bound of 2^126 follows from the 2^64 bound. The value equation turns its input condition (`< 2^260 * L`) into a condition on `Scalar52_as_Nat self`, which the caller still has to establish from its own assumptions.

I made no changes to `Curve25519Dalek/Aux.lean`.

